    [16738]={name="Witherseed Gloves",quality=2,ilvl=48,reqLevel=44,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'The Dunemaul Compound'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Andi Lynn in Tanaris. Objective: Andi Lynn in Gadgetzan wants you to destroy the Dunemaul Compound by killing 10 Dunemaul Brutes, 10 Dunemaul Enforcers, and Gor'marok the Ravager.",zone="Tanaris",questName="The Dunemaul Compound",lore="Just recently, a large band of nomadic ogres arrived in Tanaris. South of here, they have taken over a large area of the desert and formed a compound."},
    [16739]={name="Rugwood Mantle",quality=2,ilvl=48,reqLevel=44,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'The Dunemaul Compound'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Andi Lynn in Tanaris. Objective: Andi Lynn in Gadgetzan wants you to destroy the Dunemaul Compound by killing 10 Dunemaul Brutes, 10 Dunemaul Enforcers, and Gor'marok the Ravager.",zone="Tanaris",questName="The Dunemaul Compound",lore="Just recently, a large band of nomadic ogres arrived in Tanaris. South of here, they have taken over a large area of the desert and formed a compound."},
    [16741]={name="Oilrag Handwraps",quality=2,ilvl=31,reqLevel=23,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'The Lost Pages'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Gurda Ragescar in Ashenvale. Objective: Find the 12 missing pages of the Shredder Operating Manual, and put them together to form Chapters 1, 2, and 3. Return the pages to Gurda Ragescar near Splintertree Post.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="The Lost Pages",lore="I just picked up this shredder from Ratchet and I was on my way back to the Warsong Lumber Camp, where I am supposed to be on duty."},
    [16768]={name="Furbolg Medicine Pouch",quality=2,ilvl=52,sourceType="vendor",instructions="Bought from Gorn One Eye.",zone="Felwood",npc="Gorn One Eye",proc="Use: Restores 100 health every 1 sec for 10 sec. (20 Min Cooldown)"},
    [16769]={name="Furbolg Medicine Totem",quality=2,ilvl=52,reqLevel=47,sourceType="vendor",instructions="Bought from Gorn One Eye.",zone="Felwood",npc="Gorn One Eye"},
    [16788]={name="Captain Rackmore's Wheel",quality=2,ilvl=36,reqLevel=30,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Claim Rackmore's Treasure!'. The quest is in Desolace. Objective: Find Rackmore's Silver Key. Find Rackmore's Golden Key. Find and open Rackmore's Chest.",zone="Desolace",questName="Claim Rackmore's Treasure!",lore="Rackmore's log tells of how his ship was sailing for Feathermoon Stronghold when it was attacked by seafaring creatures."},
    [16791]={name="Silkstream Cuffs",quality=2,ilvl=38,reqLevel=30,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Book of the Ancients'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Azore Aldamort in Desolace. Objective: Get the Book of the Ancients and return it to Azore Aldamort at the tower in Ethel Rethor.",zone="Desolace",questName="Book of the Ancients",lore="I entrust you with the Gem of the Serpent. Place this gem on the Serpent Statue's hand on Ranazjar Isle, a small island northwest of here. Placing it will summon the one who protects the Book of the Ancients."},
    [16793]={name="Arcmetal Shoulders",quality=2,ilvl=38,reqLevel=30,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Book of the Ancients'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Azore Aldamort in Desolace. Objective: Get the Book of the Ancients and return it to Azore Aldamort at the tower in Ethel Rethor.",zone="Desolace",questName="Book of the Ancients",lore="I entrust you with the Gem of the Serpent. Place this gem on the Serpent Statue's hand on Ranazjar Isle, a small island northwest of here. Placing it will summon the one who protects the Book of the Ancients."},
    [16794]={name="Gripsteel Wristguards",quality=2,ilvl=38,reqLevel=32,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Portals of the Legion'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Taiga Wisemane in Desolace. Objective: Banish 6 Portals at Mannoroc Coven and return to Taiga Wisemane at Shadowprey Village.",zone="Desolace",questName="Portals of the Legion",lore="Behold - the Hand of Iruxos. A gruesome sight indeed. You must possess it if the demon portals at Mannoroc Coven are to be banished... which is what I now ask you to do."},
    [16873]={name="Braidfur Gloves",quality=2,ilvl=38,reqLevel=32,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Portals of the Legion'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Taiga Wisemane in Desolace. Objective: Banish 6 Portals at Mannoroc Coven and return to Taiga Wisemane at Shadowprey Village.",zone="Desolace",questName="Portals of the Legion",lore="Behold - the Hand of Iruxos. A gruesome sight indeed. You must possess it if the demon portals at Mannoroc Coven are to be banished... which is what I now ask you to do."},
    [16887]={name="Witch's Finger",quality=3,ilvl=32,reqLevel=25,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Baron Aquanis'. Pick it over the other reward choices.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="Baron Aquanis",lore="The defeated water elemental has left behind a strange water globe. You surmise that the object somehow fed the beast energy. Inside the globe, a putrid-looking form of water sloshes about."},
    [16891]={name="Claystone Shortsword",quality=2,ilvl=21,reqLevel=15,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Arachnophobia'. Pick it over the other reward choices. The quest is in Stonetalon Mountains. Objective: Kill Besseleth and bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat.",zone="Stonetalon Mountains",questName="Arachnophobia",lore="Warning: Proceed into Sishir Canyon west of here at your own risk. Besseleth and her eight-legged children of the forest have claimed this canyon as their webbed lair."},
    [16975]={name="Warsong Sash",quality=3,ilvl=27,reqLevel=22,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Warsong Supplies'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Locke Okarr in Ashenvale. Objective: Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="Warsong Supplies",lore="We are in short supply of a few items at the Warsong lumber camp!"},
    [16977]={name="Warsong Boots",quality=3,ilvl=27,reqLevel=22,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Warsong Supplies'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Locke Okarr in Ashenvale. Objective: Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="Warsong Supplies",lore="We are in short supply of a few items at the Warsong lumber camp!"},
    [16978]={name="Warsong Gauntlets",quality=3,ilvl=27,reqLevel=22,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Warsong Supplies'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Locke Okarr in Ashenvale. Objective: Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="Warsong Supplies",lore="We are in short supply of a few items at the Warsong lumber camp!"},
    [16981]={name="Owlbeard Bracers",quality=2,ilvl=20,reqLevel=14,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Earthen Arise'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Mor'rogal in Stonetalon Mountains. Objective: Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.",zone="Stonetalon Mountains",questName="Earthen Arise",lore="You have uncovered a dark threat to the land. The Resonite cask you have found in that cave houses a slumbering Earthen by the name of Goggeroc."},
    [16984]={name="Black Dragonscale Boots",quality=4,ilvl=61,reqLevel=56,sourceType="profession",instructions="Crafted with Leatherworking (requires skill 300). Bought from Lokhtos Darkbargainer.",setPiece=true,profession="Leatherworking"},
    [16986]={name="Sandspire Gloves",quality=2,ilvl=25,reqLevel=17,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'New Life'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Tammra Windfield in Stonetalon Mountains. Objective: Plant 10 Gaea Seeds in Gaea Dirt Mounds, and then return the remaining Enchanted Gaea Seeds to Tammra at Sun Rock Retreat.",zone="Stonetalon Mountains",questName="New Life",lore="As you have seen, though the land is in pain, the cycle of life is a powerful thing. Now we must do our part help it along. You must plant these seeds at the center of the destruction, to the west, in the Charred Vale."},
    [16987]={name="Screecher Belt",quality=2,ilvl=27,reqLevel=18,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Bloodfury Bloodline'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Maggran Earthbinder in Stonetalon Mountains. Objective: Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat wishes you to slay Bloodfury Ripper and bring her remains as proof of your deed.",zone="Stonetalon Mountains",questName="Bloodfury Bloodline",lore="Limiting the number of Bloodfury Harpies will not be enough. The only true cure for their disease would be to slay their leader, Bloodfury Ripper!"},
    [16990]={name="Spritekin Cloak",quality=2,ilvl=27,reqLevel=18,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Bloodfury Bloodline'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Maggran Earthbinder in Stonetalon Mountains. Objective: Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat wishes you to slay Bloodfury Ripper and bring her remains as proof of your deed.",zone="Stonetalon Mountains",questName="Bloodfury Bloodline",lore="Limiting the number of Bloodfury Harpies will not be enough. The only true cure for their disease would be to slay their leader, Bloodfury Ripper!"},
    [16995]={name="Duskwing Mantle",quality=2,ilvl=60,reqLevel=56,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'Duskwing, Oh How I Hate Thee...'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Nathanos Blightcaller in Eastern Plaguelands. Objective: Find Duskwing and slay him. From the corpse, recover a Patch of Duskwing's Fur and return it to Nathanos Blightcaller.It is said that Duskwing roams the countryside to the north of Marris Stead.",zone="Eastern Plaguelands",questName="Duskwing, Oh How I Hate Thee...",lore="Yes, imbecile, perhaps you are ready for a more involved set of missions. The albino demon bat, Duskwing, roams the countryside just north of here."},
    [16998]={name="Sacred Protector",quality=3,ilvl=62,reqLevel=56,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'The Scarlet Oracle, Demetria'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Nathanos Blightcaller in Eastern Plaguelands. Objective: The Scarlet Crusade is on the move. Somewhere along the road from Tyr's Hand to Stratholme you will find the Oracle, Demetria, and her entourage. Hunt her down and slay her. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller should you succeed.",zone="Eastern Plaguelands",questName="The Scarlet Oracle, Demetria",lore="Demetria is chief advisor to the Grand Crusader. She is called the Oracle due to her 'otherworldly' senses. She has successfully assisted the Crusade in several of their victories against the Scourge."},
    [17005]={name="Boorguard Tunic",quality=2,ilvl=27,reqLevel=21,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'King of the Foulweald'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Karang Amakkar in Ashenvale. Objective: Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound. Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner. Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="King of the Foulweald",lore="another tribe of Furbolgs, the Foulweald, live southeast of Astranaar. They are not as many as the Thistlefur, but their ferocity poses a future threat."},
    [17006]={name="Cobalt Legguards",quality=2,ilvl=27,reqLevel=21,sourceType="quest_reward",instructions="Reward from the quest 'King of the Foulweald'. Pick it over the other reward choices. Starts with Karang Amakkar in Ashenvale. Objective: Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound. Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner. Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.",zone="Ashenvale",questName="King of the Foulweald",lore="another tribe of Furbolgs, the Foulweald, live southeast of Astranaar. They are not as many as the Thistlefur, but their ferocity poses a future threat."},
